# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/

# Env / tooling
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.so

# Engine build artifacts (nethack_core is an external dependency; never vendor it here)
environments/nethack/nethack_core/
libnethack.so
dat/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.venv

# CLI-harness-eval run artifacts (tools/cli_harness_eval/launch_cell.sh):
# bulky per-turn traces, per-rollout `traces.jsonl`, eval logs and resolved
# configs from real runs. Acceptance artifacts are committed deliberately
# under tools/cli_harness_eval/acceptance/ -- these patterns don't touch
# that directory. Keep any aggregated table.md / table.json a run's
# tools/cli_harness_eval/aggregate.py produces (not matched below).
/outputs/cli_harness_eval/**/traces.jsonl
/outputs/cli_harness_eval/**/turns/
/outputs/cli_harness_eval/**/eval.log
/outputs/cli_harness_eval/**/config.toml
# Same artifacts from ANY other sweep directory. The rules above only covered
# outputs/cli_harness_eval/, so a sweep launched into a new subtree (e.g. the
# encoding-eval launcher, or a one-off probe dir) had its multi-hundred-MB
# traces show up as untracked-but-committable. Already-tracked artifacts under
# outputs/encoding_eval/ are unaffected -- .gitignore does not untrack files.
# A run's resolved config and engine provenance are OUTPUT, not source: they are
# regenerated per cell and pin a commit, so committing them puts a moving
# artifact in review. `git add -A` in a worktree that has just run an experiment
# picks them up silently -- that is how PR #36 ended up 3.4k lines of run data
# around ~1.5k of code, and it happened again on 2026-08-25.
/outputs/**/config.toml
/outputs/**/engine_provenance.json
/outputs/**/traces.jsonl
/outputs/**/turns/
/outputs/**/eval.log
# The eval CLI's default per-run dir (`<env>--<model>--<harness>/<uuid>/`)
# when `--output_dir` isn't passed explicitly (ad-hoc `eval` invocations,
# not launch_cell.sh, which always sets `--output_dir`).
/outputs/nethack_v1--*/
/outputs/*--bash/

# Task 18 Step 5: a run1 log (`outputs/cli_harness_eval/run1/prime_agent.log`)
# was committed un-ignored and carried a leaked MCP bearer token -- the Prime
# Agent arm's `ipython` tool has no denylist (see
# tools/cli_harness_eval/configs/README.md §7) and printed it into its own
# trace. Every consolidated run log under outputs/ is a raw capture of a
# real eval invocation and must never be committed, regardless of which
# subdirectory it lands in.
/outputs/**/*.log

# Core dumps. A 577MB core landed in the worktree during the hang
# investigation; large blobs like this are what previously made the branch
# unpushable (GitHub hard-fails over 100MB).
core.*
vgcore.*

# E13 run data: reproducible, large, and mutated by every run. The committed
# data branch is where results go, not the code branch.
outputs/e13/
outputs/e13_preflight/
outputs/e14_baseline/
outputs/e13_heldout/
outputs/e14_uncapped/
outputs/e15_heldout/
outputs/e15_probes/
